From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 17:06:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: meson-sm1-odroid-hc4: mux the SPI NOR HOLD# and
 WP# pins

The SPI NOR flash is wired with six lines, but nor_pins describes only
four of them - data, clock and chip select.  HOLD# (BOOT_3) and WP#
(BOOT_7) are claimed by nobody, so they keep whatever the boot ROM left
them as.  Booting from the SPI it muxes them to the nor function and the
flash works; booting from SD past the SPI - the button underneath the
board - it leaves them as eMMC data lines pulled low, and the flash stays
silent: spi-nor reports "unrecognized JEDEC id bytes: 00 00 00 00 00 00".

Claim them in a board-local group rather than adding them to nor_pins:
that group is shared with boards that keep the eMMC enabled over
BOOT_0..7, while the HC4 disables it.

Tested on ODROID-HC4: booting past the SPI, the flash now probes as mtd0
of 16 MiB and reads back correctly.

Signed-off-by: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts | 12 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts
@@ -126,13 +126,23 @@ &pwm_cd {
 
 &sd_emmc_c {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
+&periphs_pinctrl {
+	hc4_nor_hold_wp_pins: nor-hold-wp {
+		mux {
+			groups = "nor_hold", "nor_wp";
+			function = "nor";
+			bias-disable;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 &spifc {
 	status = "okay";
-	pinctrl-0 = <&nor_pins>;
+	pinctrl-0 = <&nor_pins>, <&hc4_nor_hold_wp_pins>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 
 	flash@0 {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <1>;
